# Difference Array (Range Update Optimization)

## Definition

A difference array is used to perform multiple range updates efficiently.

Instead of updating every element in a range `[l, r]`, we mark only:

- where the update starts
- where the update ends

Then we use a prefix sum to reconstruct the final array.

---

## When to Use

Use a difference array when:

- There are many range update queries.
- Queries are of the form:

  ```cpp
  arr[l...r] += val;
  ```

- You need the final array after all updates.
- Constraints are large (`N, Q ≈ 10^5` or more).

---

## Core Idea

For each update:

```cpp
arr[l...r] += val;
```

Instead of:

```cpp
for (int i = l; i <= r; i++) {
    arr[i] += val;
}
```

Do:

```cpp
diff[l] += val;

if (r + 1 < n)
    diff[r + 1] -= val;
```

After processing all queries, take the prefix sum of `diff`.

---

## Why Prefix Sum?

The difference array stores only the change in value at each index.

- `+val` at index `l` means: start adding `val`
- `-val` at index `r + 1` means: stop adding `val`

The prefix sum propagates these changes forward.

Formula:

```cpp
final[0] = diff[0];

for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    final[i] = final[i - 1] + diff[i];
}
```

---

## Example

Initial array:

```cpp
arr = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
```

Query:

```cpp
[1, 3] += 5
```

Update `diff`:

```cpp
diff[1] += 5;
diff[4] -= 5;
```

Now:

```cpp
diff = [0, 5, 0, 0, -5]
```

Prefix sum:

```text
index:  0  1  2  3  4
diff :  0  5  0  0 -5
pref :  0  5  5  5  0
```

Final array:

```cpp
arr = [0, 5, 5, 5, 0]
```

---

## Complete Template

```cpp
int n; // size of array

vector<long long> diff(n + 1, 0);

// queries: {l, r, val}
for (auto& q : queries) {
    int l = q[0];
    int r = q[1];
    long long val = q[2];

    diff[l] += val;

    if (r + 1 < n)
        diff[r + 1] -= val;
}

// Build final array using prefix sum
vector<long long> arr(n);

arr[0] = diff[0];

for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    arr[i] = arr[i - 1] + diff[i];
}
```

---

## In-Place Prefix Sum

You can reuse `diff` itself:

```cpp
for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    diff[i] += diff[i - 1];
}
```

Now:

```cpp
diff[i] == final value at index i
```

---

## Complexity

Naive approach:

```text
O(Q × N)
```

Difference array:

```text
Each update: O(1)
Build final array: O(N)

Total: O(N + Q)
```

---

## Difference Array vs Prefix Sum

### Prefix Sum

Used for:

```text
Fast range queries, slow updates.
```

Example:

```cpp
sum(l, r)
```

Time:

```text
Query: O(1)
Update: O(N)
```

---

### Difference Array

Used for:

```text
Fast range updates, final reconstruction later.
```

Example:

```cpp
arr[l...r] += val
```

Time:

```text
Update: O(1)
Final build: O(N)
```

---

## Recognition Pattern

Think of difference arrays when you see:

- Multiple range increment/decrement operations
- "Apply all operations and return final array"
- "How many intervals cover each position?"
- Large constraints (`10^5` or `10^6`)
- Offline updates (all queries known beforehand)

---

## Common Problems

- Range Addition
- Corporate Flight Bookings
- Car Pooling
- Brightness / Coverage queries
- Counting active intervals
- Railway platform overlap
- Meeting room overlap
- Population change over years
- Line sweep problems

